  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Competitor Comparison FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Competitor comparison landing pages are pages on your own site that compare your product with one named rival, row by row. They answer a search for one product against the other, or for an alternative to the rival, with a table and one next step, such as a trial.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Write down the search you want to answer, pick six to eight rows buyers decide on, and find the source for every rival claim. Then describe the page to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>. It builds the table and the form from your prompt, and each lead lands in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should the table on competitor comparison landing pages include?\", \"a\": \"The table should hold the rows a buyer decides on, each side's answer in plain words, and a source link under every rival cell. Add the date each rival cell was checked. Drop rows where both products match, unless buyers expect to see them.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I learn which features to compare on competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Ask them. Send a five-question survey to recent customers and to deals you lost, asking which tools they looked at and which difference decided it. A training software company could borrow from learning and development survey questions to hear how its buyers rank features. Emergent builds the survey from a prompt, with no response caps.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can competitor comparison landing pages name the rival brand they compare against?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The FTC's policy on comparative advertising encourages naming competitors, but requires clarity and, if necessary, disclosure to avoid deceiving the consumer. In practice, say what you compared and link the rival's own page for each claim. For anything beyond that, ask a lawyer.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make competitor comparison landing pages work on a phone?\", \"a\": \"Keep two columns on a phone: your product and one rival, with the row label above each pair of answers. Pin the column names to the top of the screen as the reader scrolls. Put a third rival behind a switch at the top instead of a sideways scroll.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which rival should I build competitor comparison landing pages against first?\", \"a\": \"Start with the rival your lost deals name first, because that page answers a question your buyers already ask. Check that people search the two names together before you write. A game studio can ask players which titles they also play with game survey questions, then compare against the one named first.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should competitor comparison landing pages be updated?\", \"a\": \"Recheck every rival cell on a fixed schedule, such as every 90 days, and again whenever a rival announces new pricing. Change the check date on the page each time. In an app Emergent builds, each check date sits in your own database, and the app can email the page owner when a cell passes its age.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should competitor comparison landing pages show the rival's prices?\", \"a\": \"Show a rival's price only when the rival publishes it, and link the public page with the date you read it. If the rival quotes prices on request, say that instead of guessing a number. A price you estimated is a claim you cannot back up.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do buyers want from competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Buyers on a comparison page already have a shortlist. They want the one difference that settles it, with proof they can open and check. To hear it from your own readers, send audience survey questions to your newsletter list before you write the rows.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 },
